rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0387756Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0400810Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0508324Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0519358Z ^[[0m
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0520123Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0521073Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0521522Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0521906Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0522828Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0523410Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0523798Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0524603Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0525021Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0525792Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0527354Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0528191Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0528614Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0528816Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0529051Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0529367Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0529626Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0530072Z    can use Nix.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0530338Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0530471Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0530656Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0531022Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0531548Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0532081Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0532281Z I will:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0532622Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0533026Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0533813Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0534291Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0534705Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0535006Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0535299Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0535719Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0536124Z    /root
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0549226Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0550180Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0561567Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0562348Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0562858Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0564060Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0564760Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0584281Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0584934Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0595253Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0596090Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0596883Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0598065Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0598417Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0598883Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0599265Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0600055Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0600460Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0600588Z If you would like to
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0600900Z see the output, try like this:
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0601106Z 
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0601325Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0601803Z   $ sh ./install-nix
rspec (ruby 4.0)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:50:13.0601975Z 
