rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7651948Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7662103Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7769636Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7780640Z ^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7781282Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7782141Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7782542Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7782878Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7783891Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7784373Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7784681Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7785343Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7785657Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7786225Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7787657Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7788491Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7788924Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7789113Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7789375Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7789678Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7789929Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7790342Z    can use Nix.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7790502Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7790621Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7790801Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7791105Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7791607Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7795699Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7795917Z I will:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7796252Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7796846Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7798047Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7798749Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7799211Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7799540Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7799854Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7800298Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7800814Z    /root
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7812312Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7813083Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7824782Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7825390Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7825859Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7827177Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7827798Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7846710Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7847320Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7857971Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7858823Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7859337Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7860003Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7860263Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7860530Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7860743Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7861176Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7861409Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7861533Z If you would like to
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7861922Z see the output, try like this:
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7862110Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7862311Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7862716Z   $ sh ./install-nix
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7862876Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7862892Z 
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7863117Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
rspec (ruby 3.4)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:37.7870840Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
