rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1218423Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1226687Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1312892Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1322343Z ^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1323000Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1323605Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1324000Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1324281Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1325520Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1326109Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1326540Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1327032Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1327275Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1327916Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1329033Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1329815Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1330366Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1330681Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1331008Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1331339Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1331660Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1332284Z    can use Nix.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1332556Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1332921Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1333152Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1333620Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1334294Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1334849Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1335424Z I will:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1335700Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1335937Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1336750Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1337098Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1337441Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1337683Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1337914Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1338245Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1338571Z    /root
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1348926Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1349505Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1359774Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1360474Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1360975Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1361682Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1362139Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1378644Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1379648Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1389098Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1389713Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1390048Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1390410Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1390577Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1390795Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1390965Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1391292Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1391535Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1391651Z If you would like to
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1391924Z see the output, try like this:
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1392123Z 
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1392306Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
rspec (ruby 3.3)	Install Nix	2026-10-08T10:49:39.1392754Z   $ sh ./install-nix
